+# home
+
+Infrastructure-as-code and documentation for our home lab and home services.
+
+The goal is simple: every service must **pay back more time than it costs**, or deliver
+clear privacy, reliability, or cost value the family can feel. No service exists just
+because it is interesting.
+
+## Repository layout
+
+```
+.
+├── as-is-analysis.md            # Current state of the home lab (keep updated)
+├── service-catalog.md           # Candidate services, requirements, value tests
+├── to-be-architecture-headless.md  # Target architecture (headless-first)
+├── docs/
+│   └── implementation-plan.md   # Phased plan + existing-service improvements + stretch goals
+├── infra/
+│   ├── desired-state/
+│   │   └── desired-state.yaml   # Desired state Arcane syncs toward
+│   ├── services/                # One compose file per service (the deployable truth)
+│   └── traefik/                 # Reverse proxy config + hot-reload dynamic routes
+├── playbooks/                   # n8n workflow definitions
+├── scripts/                     # Helper scripts (sync, verification, etc.)
+└── templates/                   # Reusable service templates
+```
+
+## How it fits together
+
+```
+Change in Git  ->  desired-state.yaml  ->  Arcane syncs  ->  Traefik routes  ->  service live
+```
+
+- **Git** is the source of truth for every service definition.
+- **desired-state.yaml** tells Arcane what should be running.
+- **Traefik** hot-reloads routes from `infra/traefik/`.
+- **Arcane** already handles container updates, so no Watchtower/duplicate tooling.
+
+## Guiding principles
+
+- Start small, prove value, then expand.
+- <5 minutes/week maintenance per service, averaged.
+- One management plane (Arcane), one proxy (Traefik).
+- Privacy by default: data stays home unless there is a compelling reason.
+- Graceful degradation: if the lab is down, family life continues.
+- If a service needs meticulous manual data entry to work, it must save more time
+  than it costs - otherwise it is a net negative.
+
+## Status
+
+Foundation phase. See `docs/implementation-plan.md` for the phased roadmap.
